Package: sloth
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-flask, nmap, adduser
Recommends: masscan, fping
Suggests: rustscan, hping3, chromium | firefox-esr
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/local/sloth
Description: Web front-end for masscan, nmap and rustscan with project storage
 Sloth is a local web application for running port scans and keeping
 the results. Scans live inside projects; each project holds tasks (one target
 range each), and findings are written to SQLite as they arrive, so closing the
 browser or restarting the service loses nothing.
 .
 Features:
  * Host discovery with 15 named probe profiles (nmap -sn variants, fping,
    masscan --ping, hping3) so dead addresses are never port-scanned.
  * Full port scans via masscan, rustscan or nmap, chosen per run. masscan
    cannot traverse IPsec/VPN tunnels; the tool detects this and warns.
  * Per-host nmap service and script scans with headless-browser screenshots
    of any web services found.
  * Live results over server-sent events, real pause/resume (SIGSTOP/SIGCONT)
    and stop that preserves masscan's resume point.
  * Self-contained HTML, TXT and JSON export per task or project.
 .
 Access requires a login; an API token is available for scripted use.
